  <knowledge>
    - Der Befehl `move obstacle` ist auf maximal zwei Paare (Schritte/Richtung) beschränkt.
    - Start fields of non-playing players remain start fields and may not be entered by other
  players.
    - Figures are brought into play in ascending order; when a figure is beaten it is appended to
  the back of the queue.
    - 'roll dice' is available while the current player has not yet rolled this turn.
    - Auf jedem Feld darf im Allgemeinen nur eine Figur stehen.
    - Wird eine Figur im Dorf geschlagen, wird sie in den Wald (`f`) gesetzt; der Wald kann nicht
  direkt betreten werden.
    - Es ist verboten, eine Figur innerhalb eines Zuges über dasselbe Feld mehrfach zu bewegen (Hin-
   und Herlaufen).
    - Wald und Dorf dürfen nur gemeinsam vorkommen; es darf maximal einen Wald geben.
    - If a session is created without a seed, the 'roll dice' command expects a parameter
  'dice_roll'.
    - The 'help' command must output a line-by-line short description of commands that are available
   in the current program state.
    - Help line format must be '<Name of command>: <Description>'.
    - Help descriptions must be in English and contain no line breaks.
    - The command 'quit' must always terminate the program and must work in every situation used for
   testing.
    - After printing an error message the program should continue and wait for the next input (do
  not exit on error).
    - Comments should be appropriate in amount and consistent in either English or German.
    - Choose meaningful identifiers for all names in the code.
    - Belegte Felder werden in `show` immer durch einen Buchstaben oder eine Zahl dargestellt.
    - Error messages must be in English and sensible.
    - When unspecified, input must come from System.in and output must go to System.out; System.err
  may be used for error messages.
    - Die Verwendung von Streams ist insbesondere zu vermeiden.
    - Alle Felder müssen horizontal und/oder vertikal verbunden sein; diagonale Nachbarschaften
  gelten nicht als Verbindung.
    - Program must be started with no command-line arguments; if an argument is passed, an error
  must be printed and the program must terminate.
    - Ein Feld darf maximal vier Nachbarn haben.
    - Players are represented by ascending lowercase letters (a, b, c, ...); player 1 is 'a', player
   2 is 'b', etc.
    - Figures are numbered before the game starting at 1 and the number remains constant throughout
  the game.
    - Wird gerade ein Hindernis bewegt (bereits gezogen, noch nicht platziert), wird das Hindernis
  nicht auf dem Spielfeld angezeigt.
    - Figuren in Schutzzonen können nicht geschlagen werden.
    - 'new figure' is available while not all a player's figures are in play and the player's start
  field is free.
    - A figure ID is the combination of the player's letter and the figure's sequential number
  (e.g., A1).
    - 'move obstacle' is available only if an obstacle has not yet been placed.
    - 'skip turn' is available if it has not been used this turn, a roll has been made, and no
  player has won.
    - 'current player' is available as long as there is no winner.
    - If a session is created with a seed, the dice roll is determined by the seed and 'roll dice'
  expects no parameter.
    - Random::nextInt(int bound) must be used to produce a value between 0 and 5; add one to obtain
  the dice result.
    - The 'help' command is always available.
    - 'move' is available if it has not been used this turn, a roll has been made this turn, and no
  player has won.
  </knowledge>
