    - Program must be started with no command-line arguments; if an argument is passed, an error
  must be printed and the program must terminate.
    - When unspecified, input must come from System.in and output must go to System.out; System.err
  may be used for error messages.
    - The 'help' command is always available.
    - The 'show' command is always available.
    - The 'quit' command must not use System.exit() or other excluded functions to terminate the
  program.
    - The help output order must be ascending (lexicographic) by command name.
    - Error messages must begin with 'Error,' and must not contain special characters such as
  newlines or umlauts.
