  <memories>
    - The document task.md describes the assignment 'Abschlussaufgabe 1 — Campus Chaos'.
    - Turn and movement rules: each player has five figures; games support up to 21 players; players
   take turns in fixed alphabetical order; on a turn a player rolls exactly once and must move
  exactly one figure the full rolled amount (no partial or backward movement); a player may
  introduce a new figure onto their start if that start is free (independent of the roll); start
  fields cannot be entered by rolling but may be traversed; landing on an opponent's figure captures
   it and returns it to the opponent's start; own figures cannot be captured; a player only skips a
  turn if no figure can be moved.
    - There is exactly one Zielfeld (target) in Campus Chaos which a player must move a figure onto
  to win.
    - task.md CONSTRAINTS the player and movement rules: each player has five pieces, up to 21
  players, turn order alphabetical ascending, a new piece may enter on an empty start (independent
  of dice), start fields cannot be entered by roll but may be traversed, each turn one roll and one
  piece must move the full roll (no partial or forward+back), pieces may be jumped (skipped fields
  count), if no piece can move the player skips turn, landing exactly on an opponent's piece
  captures it (sent back to that player's start), own pieces cannot be captured.
    - The document task.md is for the course 'Programmieren'.
    - The document task.md is for the semester 'Sommersemester 2024'.
    - ProgrammingST24-Final1 requires the CampusChaos program to be started without arguments; when
  started with no arguments it must print "Welcome to CampusChaos 2024. Enter 'help' for more
  details." and if any argument is provided the program must print an error and exit.
    - ProgrammingST24-Final1 must display the welcome message shown when started without arguments.
    - ProgrammingST24-Final1 RELATES_TO the 'start session' command which requires parameters (id,
  file, num_players, optional seed) and enforces constraints: do not overwrite existing sessions,
  file path must not contain spaces, minimum 2 players, always print the input file contents (even
  if invalid), and set the started session as active
    - ProgrammingST24-Final1 uses a 'quit' command that is available at any time to terminate the
  program.
    - ProgrammingST24-Final1 uses a 'quit' command that is available at any time, terminates the
  program without calling System.exit()/Runtime.exit(), and must work in every situation to support
  automated tests.
  </memories>
  <knowledge>
    - Der Befehl `start session` gibt bei vorhandener Datei immer zuerst den vollständigen
  Dateiinhalt zeilenweise aus, auch bei ungültigem Spielfeld.
    - Felder müssen den definierten Regeln und Abkürzungen folgen (T, P, p, O, o, Z, f,
  Spielerbuchstaben).
    - Die Eingabedatei für das Spielfeld muss eine Textdatei sein, wobei jede Zeile eine Zeile des
  Spielfeldes darstellt.
    - Fremde und eigene Figuren dürfen übersprungen werden; das übersprungene Feld wird mitgezählt.
    - 'roll dice' is available while the current player has not yet rolled this turn.
    - Wird eine Figur im Dorf geschlagen, wird sie in den Wald (`f`) gesetzt; der Wald kann nicht
  direkt betreten werden.
    - Außer Startfelder, Zielfeld und Wald muss jedes Feld mit mindestens zwei anderen Feldern
  verbunden sein.
    - If a session is created without a seed, the 'roll dice' command expects a parameter
  'dice_roll'.
    - Figures are numbered before the game starting at 1 and the number remains constant throughout
  the game.
    - Wird gerade ein Hindernis bewegt (bereits gezogen, noch nicht platziert), wird das Hindernis
  nicht auf dem Spielfeld angezeigt.
    - The number of players must be at least 2; the maximum is defined by the game board (practical
  cap stated as up to 21 players).
    - Start fields of non-playing players remain start fields and may not be entered by other
  players.
    - Figuren in Schutzzonen können nicht geschlagen werden.
    - Alle Felder müssen horizontal und/oder vertikal verbunden sein; diagonale Nachbarschaften
  gelten nicht als Verbindung.
    - 'move' is available if it has not been used this turn, a roll has been made this turn, and no
  player has won.
    - 'skip turn' is available if it has not been used this turn, a roll has been made, and no
  player has won.
